## Rust DPDK Architecture Implementation

To cleanly wrap DPDK’s C APIs into safe Rust semantics, we encapsulate the raw `rte_mbuf` pointers into RAII-managed Rust abstractions.

### 1. High-Performance Packet Ingestion Loop

Below is a simplified architecture showing an idiomatic Rust abstraction wrapping DPDK burst polling:

```rust
use std::ffi::CString;
use std::ptr;

// FFI binding abstractions for DPDK
pub struct PacketBuffer {
    mbuf_ptr: *mut dpdk_sys::rte_mbuf,
}

impl PacketBuffer {
    #[inline(always)]
    pub fn data(&self) -> &[u8] {
        unsafe {
            let data_ptr = (*self.mbuf_ptr).buf_addr.add((*self.mbuf_ptr).data_off as usize) as *const u8;
            let data_len = (*self.mbuf_ptr).data_len as usize;
            std::slice::from_raw_parts(data_ptr, data_len)
        }
    }
}

impl Drop for PacketBuffer {
    #[inline(always)]
    fn drop(&mut self) {
        unsafe {
            dpdk_sys::rte_pktmbuf_free(self.mbuf_ptr);
        }
    }
}

pub struct RxQueue {
    port_id: u16,
    queue_id: u16,
}

impl RxQueue {
    #[inline(always)]
    pub fn rx_burst(&self, rx_pkts: &mut [*mut dpdk_sys::rte_mbuf; 32]) -> u16 {
        unsafe {
            dpdk_sys::rte_eth_rx_burst(
                self.port_id,
                self.queue_id,
                rx_pkts.as_mut_ptr(),
                rx_pkts.len() as u16,
            )
        }
    }
}
```

### 2. Lock-Free Zero-Copy Processing Loop

To maximize throughput across NUMA nodes, trading engines pin worker threads directly to dedicated CPU cores (`core_affinity`).

```rust
pub fn process_market_feed(rx_queue: RxQueue) {
    let mut burst_buffer: [*mut dpdk_sys::rte_mbuf; 32] = [ptr::null_mut(); 32];

    loop {
        // Poll NIC ring buffer directly (0 context switches)
        let nb_rx = rx_queue.rx_burst(&mut burst_buffer);

        if nb_rx == 0 {
            // Core busy-polls; no sleeping or yield to kernel
            std::hint::spin_loop();
            continue;
        }

        for i in 0..nb_rx as usize {
            let pkt = PacketBuffer { mbuf_ptr: burst_buffer[i] };
            let payload = pkt.data();

            // Fast-path parsing of ITCH / SBE market data frames
            parse_and_evaluate_orderbook(payload);

            // `pkt` goes out of scope here and automatically triggers DPDK buffer release
        }
    }
}
```

